--TEST--
"for" tag condition: loop.* variables work correctly inside the body

In Twig 1.x/2.x the legacy implementation wrapped the body in an "if" so
loop.last and loop.length could not be relied on (see the original
loop_not_defined.test). The reintroduced implementation desugars to
"seq|filter(...)", so the foreach iterates over the already-filtered
sequence and loop.* reflects post-filter counts correctly.
--TEMPLATE--
{% for i, item in items if i > 0 -%}
{{ i }}={{ item }} (last={{ loop.last ? 'y' : 'n' }}, length={{ loop.length }})
{% endfor %}
--DATA--
return ['items' => ['a', 'b', 'c']]
--EXPECT--
1=b (last=n, length=2)
2=c (last=y, length=2)
